MENTOR: Glow is a good choice. Its animated property sits inside an effect, not under Transform, so it's a little different from the others.

Glow has only **one pair**: **Effects › Gaussian Blur › Blurriness, from 0 s to 1 s.** If I eased it for you, there'd be nothing left for you to do. So instead of a demo, I'll talk you through it, and you do the clicking.

Above is 0.5 s, the middle of that pair. Right now the blur changes at exactly the same rate the whole second, then stops dead at 1 s. Easing makes it start gently, speed up in the middle, and settle into the final value.

**Steps:**
1. In the timeline, select the **Glow** layer and press **U**. This shows only the animated properties, so Blurriness will appear without you digging through Effects.
2. Click the keyframe at 0 s, then Shift-click the one at 1 s so both are selected.
3. Press **F9** (or use **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease**).
4. Check it: both diamonds should turn into hourglass shapes. For a closer look, open the **Graph Editor** (the small graph button above the layers). A flat-then-steep-then-flat curve means it's eased.

Say **"done"** when you've tried it and I'll check.

Or, if you'd rather watch me do one first, we can switch to **Title**. It has four pairs, so I can ease one and leave the other three for you.
